-- Row il-79. THE REFERENCES, as typed values: item I1 (section 38 of the Law and the numbers printed beside the two enactments it cites) and item I2 (the definition of "the court" in section 1, the instruction SH 2760 prints on it, and the appeal provisions of the Courts Law as printed).
-- Tests of the controls are in ab79-tests-controls.l4, and the assertions that FAIL on purpose (four: three for I1, one for I2) are in ab79-tests-red.l4.
--
-- THE QUOTATION LINES.
-- `src:N` lines are expanded mechanically from the excerpt of the Hebrew Wikisource consolidation (UNOFFICIAL, so CONSOLIDATION-ONLY) by tools/srcquote.py; N is the line number in the whole page, which the excerpt's header lists.
-- `ext:[tag] | ...` lines quote the Hebrew read from the deposited page image of an official instrument (Sefer HaChukim (SH) issue NNNN, or Dinei Medinat Yisrael, New Version 19 (NV 19)); the tag names the instrument and the printed page (registers/source-bundle/pages/). Footnote numbers, and the quotation marks a page prints around an inserted text, are left out of the quoted lines. A table row is quoted as `previous | new`, the number printed under the heading "the previous section" and the number printed under the heading "the new section".
-- `tr:[tag] | LATIN` lines give the Latin form of words quoted on the lines above them, and tools/translit.py checks them against the Hebrew and against the string literals below.
-- Nothing is quoted from memory. Every date, number and section below is on a quotation line or in NOTES.md.
-- A date typed as `the issue date its footer prints` is the date of the issue, and it is never a day of effect. No page deposited prints a day of effect for any instrument.
-- The row does not say whether any of the provisions of the Interpretation Law typed below bears on the citing words.

§ `References`

